KG42.register("source_edge_archive-21e62f6d9225a756952804ba",{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E001","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-bebd346528bbcf18","target":"COMP-6057789601b08e93","source_occurrence_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","target_occurrence_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","target_unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"dfb541186cbabbd6d47411bc75d6b92c5867f6cdccb90b28152b69d8ac9b0d6e","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The auctioneer determines the price paid for sharing RU storage, with the stated objective of maximizing average SFC cost savings while satisfying their storage needs. Scope: Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. Stackelberg coordination of RU decisions in response to the auctioneer's announced price facilitates determination of the storage-sharing auction price in the payment rule. Scope: Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction. The number of participating RUs identified by the determination rule informs determination of the auction price through the Stackelberg payment rule. Scope: Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. The determination rule selects the participating RUs and SFCs before the payment rule determines the auction price. Scope: Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. The auction-price strategy is restricted to [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] in the strategy-set and algorithm formulations. Scope: Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1.","target_definition":"The auction price is the price SFC customers must pay RU owners for sharing their ES devices. Scope: The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The auction price is the price SFC customers must pay RU owners for sharing their ES devices. Scope: The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x-p_t"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"ED APPROACH 1467 its In the proposed approach, each RU i iteratively responds to the to strategy pt ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"]},"paper_scope_note":"Initial selection boundary, removal of marginal participants, Stackelberg price, and spatial response are kept separate; this is limited to component use in this auction protocol and does not prove a unique equilibrium or real-world operation."}});
